--TEST--
A `Core\Time::sleep` that would end past `[limits] wall_time` ends when the time runs out, and the request stops with a limit report naming `wall_time` — `rule:errors/on-limit`
--FILE nvs.toml--
# The run may take 300 milliseconds from start to end.
[limits]
wall_time = "300ms"
--FILE--
<?nvs
Core\Fatal::onLimit(fn (array<string> $report): void => {
    echo "onLimit ", $report['limit'], "\n";
});

// The sleep ends when the wall time runs out, so the request stops there.
echo "sleeping\n";
Core\Time::sleep(Core\Time\Duration::seconds(30));
echo "not reached\n";
--EXPECT--
sleeping
onLimit wall_time
--EXPECT-ERROR--
FATAL: the request exceeded its wall-time limit of 300ms
